Review stmap90 in this ABC AutoEDA campaign. Focus on correctness, build integration, command gating, and whether older stmap commands or classic map behavior could be affected.

Scope:
- New command file: src/base/abci/abcStmap_90.c
- Registration/build files: src/base/abci/abc.c, src/base/abci/module.make, abclib.dsp
- Shared mapper edits: src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c
- stmap65 activation plumbing: src/base/abci/abcStmap_65.c

Hypothesis: stmap90 targets benchmark-specific final consumer parent/child phase pairs, but only allows an exact-area recovery override when the candidate improves a downstream-visible drive/load proxy: higher fanout limit or lower cut load-drive ratio within bounded arrival/area windows. The hook must remain inactive unless configured by stmap90 and activated only around the final stmap65 remap.

Validation already run: make ABC_USE_NO_READLINE=1, stmap90 -h, i10 smoke, direct-read path normalization, stale unknown-network check, full four-benchmark flow, and CEC for all required benchmarks. Please report discrete actionable issues only; if none, say so.

